# The fusions whose parts carry a conversion nobody sized. One row per such fusion, shaped like the
# two elimination suspensions beside it, so the union stays a union.
#
# A derived conversion is said to be one
#   A derivation is an output the receiver computes, not a gap. Nothing computes a factor from the
#   rest of the unit graph or from the fusion's sum, so the sum is still suspended, under the
#   identity's name.
#
# The same reason an unsized elimination suspends the sum
#   The schema makes the argument about eliminations: "an entry whose `quantity` takes its absent
#   branch is a composer who found the overlap and could not size it, so the sum is lifted exactly
#   where the elimination was filed." A factor is the other multiplier in the converted parts added
#   up. If nobody sized it, the converted part is not a number, and the sum it feeds is not owed.
#
# It keeps composition/converted.sqlc from counting short
#   composition/converted.sqlc drops a part whose factor is a typed blank, because converting it by
#   one would assert the units agree, the claim the filer declined to make. A dropped part in a sum
#   that still owes equality is a shortfall the check invented. This is the ground that keeps the
#   two consistent.
#
# Its one fusion is already suspended on another ground
#   `every-unsized-conversion/shift-capacity` is the only such fusion, and it files its elimination
#   search as `unmeasured` too, so no verdict moves on this corpus. This makes structural something
#   that is true only by luck, as every CHECK in the DDL does.
-- asrt:Part/asrt:factor taking its pm:absent or pm:derivation branch, as a suspension of the
-- composed sum.
SELECT p.composition, p.composed_layer,
       NULL::pm.summed_quantity AS quantity,
       CASE WHEN p.factor_state = 'derivation'
            THEN format('the conversion is filed as `%s`, and no computation of it is wired into '
                        'the sum', p.factor_derivation)
            ELSE 'the conversion was filed and could not be sized' END AS suspended_because,
       coalesce(p.factor_absent::text, p.factor_derivation::text) AS note
FROM (
    :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
) p
WHERE p.factor_state IN ('absent', 'derivation')
